Verify kernel.json against current_kernel, skill, memory, and exclude_skills in the
generation record. Load the input Kernel from its directory or inline dictionary.
Convert directory/card path strings to Path and reconstruct inline SkillCards
before calling Python functions.
Do not modify upstream files, candidate sources, or cards.

When skill is supplied, load that exact card with the registered load_skill or
SkillCard.from_dict and verify its application. No memory selection is required.

When skill is null, recompute candidates using klineage.agent_tools.retrieve with
the original memory and exclusions. This only filters scope and excluded IDs;
check textual prerequisites and already-present mechanisms against the input source.
If candidates existed, inspect the generation's actual profile request, result,
metrics, and report. Require matching kernel fingerprint/problem and source-grounded
ranking. Missing, stale, or unsupported measurements mean false.

- With SKILL.md, require exactly one unchanged card from those candidates. Reject
  excluded or inapplicable cards, invented recipes, and unsupported ranking claims.
- Without SKILL.md, require the input kernel to be preserved exactly and no
  submission/. Accept only if no candidate applies, with reasons for every rejection.
  Finish without fabricating a new measured validation for unchanged artifacts.

For an application, require the complete problem and ABI to match the input and submission/ to match
source_files.
{% include "backend.j4" %}
Audit the selected backend's bundle; for Python, check the configured callable and
output convention. Inspect actual code for the card's scope,
preconditions, intent, body and preserved mechanisms. Check types, layout/contiguity
and parallel ownership, storage placement, pipeline stages/ordering, and hardware
features on the input. Reject additional unrelated
optimizations.

Use .agents/skills/bench/SKILL.md and klineage.harness.evaluate(candidate, workdir,
reference=current_kernel). Require ValidationResult.accepted, including the paired
performance gate. Record measurements and source citations under evaluations/ and
attach only measured validation to kernel.json. Missing evidence or unavailable tools
mean false; do not fabricate speedups or passed checks.

